Splosh contains the third-party material below, which keeps its own license.


Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash) and its fork Splish
(https://github.com/publicExcess/splish)

The way Splosh runs GGUF weights is adapted from Splash and Splish:

- Sources/Shaders/gguf_formats.h: the plane encoding, the chunk order and the
  per-format decoders, from runtime/metal/abi/QuantFormat.h,
  kernels/common/quant_formats.h and kernels/common/gguf_staged.h.
- Sources/SploshModel/GgufPlanes.swift: the encoding the weights are repacked
  into, from runtime/metal/abi/QuantFormat.h and
  kernels/shared/gguf_repack.metal, re-tiled from 256 rows to 128.
- Sources/Shaders/engine_gguf.metal: decoding a block of weights into
  threadgroup memory before each product, as in
  kernels/common/gguf_staged_tile.h and kernels/shared/gguf_linear.metal.

Each of those files says in its header what it takes and what was changed.
